# Activity 04 - Flower Catalog

A responsive web application showcasing a catalog of flowers using Bootstrap 5.

## Author

- **Name:** Evan Litzer
- **Email:** bubaq@iastate.edu
- **Date:** September 11, 2025
- **Course:** CS319 - Construction of User Interfaces

## Description

This project displays a collection of flowers in an album-style layout. Each flower is presented in a card format with an image and descriptive text about the species. The catalog includes:

- Lily (*Lilium candidum*)
- Daisy (*Leucanthemum vulgare*)
- Blue Lotus (*Nymphaea caerulea*)
- Bluebell (*Hyacinthoides*)
- Sunflower (*Helianthus annuus*)
- Tulip (*Tulipa*)

## Features

- **Responsive Grid Layout:** Cards automatically adjust from 1 to 3 columns based on screen size
- **Theme Toggle:** Light, dark, and auto theme modes
- **Collapsible Navigation:** Header with expandable about/contact section
- **Bootstrap 5.3:** Modern UI components and styling

## Project Structure

```
Activity04/
├── index.html          # Main webpage
├── images/             # Flower images and descriptions
│   ├── *.jpg           # Flower photographs
│   └── *.txt           # Text descriptions for each flower
└── README.md           # This file
```

## Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Bootstrap 5.3.8 (CDN)
- JavaScript (Bootstrap Bundle)

## How to Run

1. Open `index.html` in a web browser
2. Or serve the directory using a local web server

## Dependencies

The project uses Bootstrap via CDN, so an internet connection is required for full styling and functionality.
